WEBVTT

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.865
For our third course...

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.102
Another course!

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.339
Luhvian quail in truffle sauce,

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.610
served with roasted chadre kab.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.714
My compliments to the chef.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:22.914
Hear, hear.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.821
Thank you, Captain.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.623
Cream of leola soup, fettran
risotto, Luhvian quail...

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.186
it just keeps getting better.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.129
I knew you'd been
expanding your palate,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.633
but I didn't realize
you'd become a gourmet cook.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:39.832
Preparing meals myself is
the best way to ensure quality.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.771
I suppose I should be insulted,

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.741
but everything is so delicious,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.246
I may just have to admit defeat
and hang up my apron.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.578
No, that'd be a real tragedy,
Neelix.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.476
Pinot noir, Commander?

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.521
I'll have another glass
of the chardonnay.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.954
Each course has been paired
with a specific wine.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.651
Substitutions
are not recommended.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:02.024
The pinot noir sounds perfect.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.585
Is there any salt?

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.598
Additional seasoning
is not required.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.099
Oh, I'm sorry, I...

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.534
If the quail hasn't been
prepared to your satisfaction,

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.867
I could replicate something
more to your liking.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.930
A peanut butter
and jelly sandwich, perhaps.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:18.876
Actually, it's delicious
just the way it is.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.808
Captain to the Bridge.
Report.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.146
We're being pulled off-course.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.208
How?

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.549
I'm not certain.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.953
It appears to be
some kind of graviton surge.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.956
On my way.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.955
We've rerouted all available
power to the thrusters,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.590
but we can't break free.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.397
Try reversing
the shield polarity.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.459
No effect.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.254
What happened to the stars?

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.575
Shields at 65 percent!

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.735
Hail them.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.244
They're not responding.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.779
Return fire.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.911
Can you identify them?

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.885
Their weapon signature
is Vaadwaur,

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.751
but the ship has technology
from several different species.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.381
There's another vessel
approaching.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.392
It's charging weapons.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.121
Evasive pattern Beta-6.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.934
Maybe we've got an ally.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.698
The Vaadwaur ship is retreating.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.102
Hail the second ship.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.739
No response.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.904
I stand corrected.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:47.251
They have penetrated
our aft shields.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.880
Reroute power to the auxiliary
emitters and return fire.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.128
They've transported material
off Decks 5, 7 and 8.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.793
Disable their engines.

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:10.276
Follow them.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.243
Navigational sensors
are malfunctioning.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:14.143
Something to do
with this environment.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.181
I want a full damage report
and an inventory

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.217
of everything that was
taken off this ship.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.911
And I want to know where we are.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.420
They got more than 90 percent
of our food stores,

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.389
including almost everything
in the Airponics Bay.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.892
They also got a computer console
from Engineering,

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.554
and they emptied three
of our deuterium tanks.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.723
Why would anyone
steal deuterium?

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.460
You could find it anywhere.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.468
Apparently not here.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.935
I'm not detecting any gases,

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.130
stellar bodies,
or matter of any kind.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:42.299
Except for the ships
that attacked us.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.672
Scan for other vessels.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.177
I want to know how many
we're dealing with.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.805
There are more than 150 ships
within scanning range,

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.349
but I'm only detecting
life signs on 29 of them.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.284
Captain, there's another vessel
approaching at high impulse.

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.117
Quite a welcoming committee
they've got here.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.850
What's the status
of our shields?

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:58.948
They're at 28 percent.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.457
That'll have to do.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:01.618
Charge weapons.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.389
Captain, this one wants to talk.

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:05.795
On screen.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:08.191
I'm Captain Janeway

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.360
of the Starship Voyager.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.404
General Valen.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.235
Welcome to the Void.

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.538
You're the first ship
we've seen here

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.078
that hasn't tried to fire on us,

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.408
but in case you change
your mind,

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:23.472
we're prepared
to defend ourselves.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.245
I know; I've been observing you
on sensors.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:29.550
The way you fought those ships
was impressive.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:32.682
Most vessels don't survive
the first few minutes.

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:36.058
I'd appreciate any information
you could give us

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:38.393
about where we are.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:41.126
The anomaly's
a closed structure,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.260
encased by an inert layer
of subspace.

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:46.737
Matter and energy
can't penetrate it.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:49.036
Our ships certainly
penetrated it

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.700
when we were pulled in.

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:52.642
By the funnels.

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:57.407
But they only pull matter
in one direction:

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.916
Into the Void.

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.579
Have you explored
the entire anomaly?

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.316
There's nothing to explore,
but it's big.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.984
We've calculated
the outer circumference

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.254
at approximately
nine light-years,

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.626
but we've never been able
to breach it.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:12.527
How long have you been here?

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:16.297
More than five years.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.633
There must be a way to escape.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:21.298
New arrivals are always
thinking about escape.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:25.276
We have
a sophisticated starship.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:28.370
Maybe if we work together,
we can find a way out.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.279
You're being naive.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.374
No one ever gets out.

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.818
We may be able
to devise a new approach.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.582
Many have tried.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.248
All they did was waste resources

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.918
that could've
kept them alive longer.

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:42.426
Don't be foolish.

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:44.224
I can help you.

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.594
How?

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:48.133
The only source
of food and energy in the Void

00:07:48.201 --> 00:07:50.328
comes from new ships
that are drawn in.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.768
If you want to survive here,

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:55.239
you'll have to compete
for their resources.

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:58.607
And I suppose
you can help us do that.

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:01.374
I have tactical data

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.506
on some of the more dangerous
predators.

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:06.848
But you want something
in return.

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:12.248
My scans show
you have photon torpedoes.

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:15.590
I'm sorry,
we don't trade weapons.

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.026
Why not?

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:18.393
Because we have
no way of knowing

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:20.056
what they'll be used for.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:23.590
Plundering innocent ships,
for example.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:27.537
Wait a few weeks until
your resources start to run out.

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:30.804
Morality won't keep your
life support systems running.

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:32.139
I'm sorry, General.

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:34.941
There are some compromises
I won't make.

00:08:36.816 --> 00:08:38.613
Not yet.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:54.594
Report, Lieutenant.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:58.068
We're using power at almost
ten times the usual rate.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:08:59.661
While we're standing still?

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:02.173
The same graviton forces
that pulled us into the anomaly

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:03.765
seem to be draining
the warp core.

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:07.870
At this rate, our deuterium
will be gone in about ten days.

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:10.141
Shut down all
nonessential systems.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:11.274
Where are you going?

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.478
To find a way out of here.

00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:17.079
Using fractal algorithms
with the Borg sensors,

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:18.885
I believe I can predict
where and when

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.391
these funnels will occur.

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:23.223
Well, that's impressive,
but how does it help us?

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:25.890
The funnels originate
inside the anomaly,

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:29.025
creating massive graviton forces
before they erupt.

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.399
If we were to enter
one of the funnels

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.165
just as that happened,

00:09:33.239 --> 00:09:34.831
we might be able
to use those forces

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:36.272
to propel us into normal space.

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:38.902
Not without compromising
structural integrity.

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:41.776
I might be able to reinforce
the shields to compensate.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.337
There's another problem.

00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:46.476
When the graviton forces
reach critical levels,

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:48.577
the polarity suddenly reverses,

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:49.916
pulling everything
near the funnel

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:51.217
back into the anomaly.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.758
We'd have to jump to warp
at exactly the right moment.

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:56.852
We'd need to achieve
a velocity of warp 8.2.

00:09:56.929 --> 00:10:00.296
Question is,
will we have enough power?

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:02.095
At the rate we're losing it...

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:06.769
...we may only get
one shot at this.

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:09.137
The sooner we try, the better.

00:10:15.348 --> 00:10:19.307
There's a funnel forming
70,000 meters off the port bow...

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:21.182
bearing 130 mark 24.

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.881
Graviton surge in 34 seconds.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:26.857
Full power to shields
and structural integrity.

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:28.757
Take us in, Mr. Paris.

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:34.765
Five seconds...

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:35.892
four...

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.060
three...

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:44.171
Structural integrity
at 20 percent.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.147
Ten percent!

00:10:52.551 --> 00:10:54.416
50,000 kilometers
to normal space.

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:55.749
Prepare to go to warp.

00:11:18.611 --> 00:11:20.875
Engineering to the Bridge.

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:22.106
Go ahead.

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:24.979
The warp core is off-line.

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:35.619
If nothing else,
we learned some things

00:11:35.695 --> 00:11:37.458
that'll help us next time.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.622
With all due respect, Captain,

00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:40.632
we don't even have
warp drive anymore.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.463
I may be able
to get it back on line,

00:11:42.535 --> 00:11:43.797
but we still need deuterium

00:11:43.869 --> 00:11:45.803
to keep our basic systems
running.

00:11:45.871 --> 00:11:47.463
How long will our reserves last?

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.304
If we shut down life support
on all but a few decks,

00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:52.139
deactivate Astrometrics,
turbolifts,

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:55.806
ration replicator
use... maybe a week.

00:11:55.881 --> 00:11:58.315
I used to make a living
scavenging for supplies.

00:11:58.384 --> 00:11:59.817
Let me take one of the shuttles.

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:01.750
I might be able to find
deuterium

00:12:01.821 --> 00:12:03.083
on one of those abandoned ships.

00:12:03.155 --> 00:12:05.089
A shuttle would be
too easy a target.

00:12:05.157 --> 00:12:06.590
I appreciate the offer, Neelix,

00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:08.251
but we're safer
if we stay together.

00:12:08.327 --> 00:12:10.591
The shuttles may be useful
in another capacity.

00:12:10.663 --> 00:12:14.030
We could use their warp cores
to augment power on Voyager.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.330
We're still going to need
more deuterium.

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:20.934
Let's track down
the ship that raided us

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.531
and get back what they stole.

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:24.837
We should do it quickly.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.401
I've detected a number
of vessels monitoring us.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.380
The vultures are circling.

00:12:29.448 --> 00:12:31.848
Vultures eat the dead,
Mr. Paris.

00:12:31.917 --> 00:12:34.852
We're not dead yet.

00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:41.959
The vessel's in visual range.

00:12:42.061 --> 00:12:43.323
Shields.

00:12:43.395 --> 00:12:46.887
On screen.

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:51.366
Looks like somebody got to them
before we did.

00:12:51.437 --> 00:12:53.098
No life signs.

00:12:53.172 --> 00:12:54.366
Scan for ion trails.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:57.068
Whoever did this
probably has our deuterium.

00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:58.610
Aye, Captain.

00:12:58.677 --> 00:13:01.805
Is there anything left aboard
that ship worth salvaging?

00:13:01.881 --> 00:13:05.282
Their technology and supplies
have been picked clean.

00:13:05.351 --> 00:13:07.478
Not everything of value
has been taken.

00:13:07.553 --> 00:13:09.214
The warp core has been removed,

00:13:09.288 --> 00:13:11.654
but the casing
that protected it is intact.

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:13.248
It's composed of tricesium.

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:15.919
We can convert it
into a power source.

00:13:16.028 --> 00:13:17.461
Every little bit helps.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:20.931
Lock onto the core casing
and beam it to the Cargo Bay.

00:13:21.066 --> 00:13:22.465
With the additional power,

00:13:22.535 --> 00:13:24.799
we could reactivate
the Astrometrics Lab.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.633
I can think of some better uses.

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:27.637
For example?

00:13:27.706 --> 00:13:28.764
Oh, I don't know...

00:13:28.841 --> 00:13:31.002
making sure
there's air to breathe.

00:13:46.859 --> 00:13:49.384
This must be where they cut
through the casing

00:13:49.461 --> 00:13:50.723
to remove the core.

00:13:50.796 --> 00:13:52.957
Crude but effective.

00:13:56.502 --> 00:13:58.970
Something's in there.

00:13:59.038 --> 00:14:00.437
Identify yourself.

00:14:01.207 --> 00:14:03.004
Torres to Security.

00:14:03.075 --> 00:14:04.508
Intruder alert.

00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:06.169
Acknowledged.

00:14:09.348 --> 00:14:10.610
There.

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:12.116
Stay where you are.

00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:17.617
He appears to be injured.

00:14:29.702 --> 00:14:31.169
How is he?

00:14:31.237 --> 00:14:32.932
His injury doesn't seem serious,

00:14:33.005 --> 00:14:35.974
but he won't let me
close enough to treat him.

00:14:39.578 --> 00:14:41.739
My name's Captain Janeway.

00:14:41.814 --> 00:14:43.213
You're safe here.

00:14:43.282 --> 00:14:45.512
I've tried
communicating with him.

00:14:45.584 --> 00:14:47.950
He doesn't appear to
have any verbal skills.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:49.681
Do we know how he got on board?

00:14:49.755 --> 00:14:52.781
I believe he was transported
along with the core casing.

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:55.190
We should have
picked up his life signs.

00:14:55.261 --> 00:14:58.287
We're trying to determine
why we didn't detect him.

00:14:58.364 --> 00:15:00.730
That vessel he was on
had no atmosphere.

00:15:00.799 --> 00:15:01.891
How did he survive?

00:15:02.001 --> 00:15:04.367
My scans show
he can conserve oxygen.

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:06.199
He has unusually large
lung capacity

00:15:06.272 --> 00:15:07.830
and a voracious appetite.

00:15:07.907 --> 00:15:10.273
Do you think
that ship was his home?

00:15:10.342 --> 00:15:12.469
Maybe, but we can't
send him back.

00:15:12.544 --> 00:15:16.480
He can't survive without
oxygen indefinitely.

00:15:16.548 --> 00:15:18.880
We'll run scans for other
members of his species,

00:15:18.951 --> 00:15:21.476
but until we can find
a safe place for him,

00:15:21.553 --> 00:15:23.822
let's make him
as comfortable as possible.

00:15:26.659 --> 00:15:29.628
Computer, replicate a portion
of nutritional supplements

00:15:29.695 --> 00:15:30.992
from my daily allotment.

00:15:40.372 --> 00:15:41.930
You've found something?

00:15:42.007 --> 00:15:44.942
We think we know
who has our deuterium.

00:15:45.044 --> 00:15:47.979
It's someone we've already met.

00:15:50.916 --> 00:15:52.941
I knew I'd see you again,
Captain.

00:15:53.018 --> 00:15:56.613
I expect you've reconsidered
my proposal.

00:15:56.689 --> 00:15:58.179
We're not here to trade.

00:15:58.257 --> 00:16:00.953
We're here to take back
what belongs to us.

00:16:01.026 --> 00:16:02.618
I don't know what you mean.

00:16:02.695 --> 00:16:05.596
Our scans indicate
you've got some of our food,

00:16:05.664 --> 00:16:06.892
one of our consoles,

00:16:06.999 --> 00:16:09.297
and a large quantity
of our deuterium.

00:16:09.368 --> 00:16:11.302
We didn't take
any of that from you.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:14.567
No, apparently you killed
the crew of another ship

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.232
and took it from them.

00:16:16.308 --> 00:16:17.775
We want it back.

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:20.311
That's not the way
things work here.

00:16:20.379 --> 00:16:23.815
Either you give it back,
or we'll take it.

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:28.715
He's powering his engines.

00:16:28.787 --> 00:16:31.585
Target his shields and fire.

00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:35.085
Lock onto whatever belongs to us

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.457
and transport it
to the cargo bay.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:41.596
I'm detecting large quantities
of food on his supply deck.

00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:43.794
Maybe we should take it
while we have the chance.

00:16:43.869 --> 00:16:45.598
Is it ours?

00:16:45.671 --> 00:16:47.434
No, but our own reserves
are running out.

00:16:47.506 --> 00:16:51.306
Valen wouldn't hesitate
to take it from us.

00:16:51.377 --> 00:16:53.311
No, he wouldn't.

00:16:53.379 --> 00:16:54.903
We've got what's ours.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.277
Reverse course.

00:17:09.328 --> 00:17:10.920
Come in.

00:17:13.332 --> 00:17:15.596
An updated inventory
of our supplies.

00:17:15.667 --> 00:17:18.602
We got back less than half
of what was stolen.

00:17:20.939 --> 00:17:23.533
Doesn't take two of you
to deliver a padd.

00:17:23.609 --> 00:17:24.803
What's on your mind?

00:17:26.545 --> 00:17:27.603
We want to be clear

00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:29.340
about what our policy's
going to be

00:17:29.415 --> 00:17:30.814
while we're here in the Void.

00:17:30.883 --> 00:17:34.046
You think we should
have taken Valen's food.

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:36.587
Logic suggests we may have to be

00:17:36.655 --> 00:17:38.919
more opportunistic
if we intend to survive.

00:17:38.991 --> 00:17:40.925
We may not like Valen's tactics,

00:17:40.993 --> 00:17:42.756
but he and his crew
are still alive

00:17:42.828 --> 00:17:44.318
after five years in here.

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:46.626
I was thinking
about that myself.

00:17:48.367 --> 00:17:50.426
I thought maybe
I could get some guidance

00:17:50.502 --> 00:17:52.470
from the Federation Charter.

00:17:53.672 --> 00:17:57.267
I was hoping I'd find a loophole
that would allow us to...

00:17:57.342 --> 00:18:00.402
take actions
we ordinarily wouldn't take.

00:18:00.479 --> 00:18:02.208
Any luck?

00:18:02.281 --> 00:18:04.772
The Charter's
a statement of principles,

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.477
not a practical document.

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:09.043
No section on how to exist
in a void.

00:18:09.121 --> 00:18:10.418
No.

00:18:12.124 --> 00:18:13.421
But I've become convinced

00:18:13.492 --> 00:18:15.653
that we've got to stick
to our principles,

00:18:15.727 --> 00:18:16.989
not abandon them.

00:18:17.062 --> 00:18:19.496
Should the crew be ready
to die for those principles?

00:18:19.565 --> 00:18:21.089
If the alternative means

00:18:21.166 --> 00:18:23.896
becoming thieves
and killers ourselves, yes.

00:18:24.002 --> 00:18:26.197
But I'm betting
that our principles

00:18:26.271 --> 00:18:28.034
are going to keep us alive.

00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:29.233
Captain?

00:18:29.308 --> 00:18:33.608
The Federation is based
on mutual cooperation...

00:18:33.679 --> 00:18:35.647
the idea that the whole
is greater

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:37.272
than the sum of its parts.

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:39.840
Voyager can't
survive here alone,

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:43.911
but if we form a temporary
alliance with other ships,

00:18:44.022 --> 00:18:46.582
maybe we can pool
our resources and escape.

00:18:46.658 --> 00:18:48.023
As you've pointed out,

00:18:48.093 --> 00:18:50.493
the people we've encountered
in this void

00:18:50.562 --> 00:18:51.927
are thieves and killers.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:54.931
Such individuals
are hardly ideal allies.

00:18:55.033 --> 00:18:56.728
I agree.

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:59.703
Then who are we going
to form an alliance with?

00:18:59.771 --> 00:19:03.207
Anyone who agrees
to play by our rules:

00:19:03.275 --> 00:19:07.644
No killing, no stealing,
and no giving up.

00:19:07.713 --> 00:19:08.975
Forgive me, Captain,

00:19:09.047 --> 00:19:11.140
but why would anyone
who has survived

00:19:11.216 --> 00:19:14.413
by killing and stealing
suddenly agree to those terms?

00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:18.479
We'll offer to share
our food and medical supplies

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:22.254
and defend ships
that are attacked by raiders.

00:19:22.327 --> 00:19:25.888
Captain, maybe you'd better take
another look at that inventory.

00:19:26.031 --> 00:19:29.262
Our food and power reserves
will be gone within a week.

00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:31.461
If we start giving
everything away...

00:19:31.537 --> 00:19:34.904
Then maybe we'll only survive
for two days instead of seven.

00:19:34.973 --> 00:19:36.907
On the other hand,
if we share what we have,

00:19:37.042 --> 00:19:38.737
instead of hoarding it,

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.677
we might find other people
willing to do the same.

00:19:41.747 --> 00:19:43.442
If we combine our technology,

00:19:43.515 --> 00:19:46.416
we can find ways
of improving our situation

00:19:46.485 --> 00:19:50.922
and ultimately
get the hell out of this place.

00:19:50.989 --> 00:19:53.924
We may lose a little weight,
gentlemen,

00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:57.621
but we won't lose who we are.

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:06.263
Captain's Log, Stardate 54553.4.

00:20:06.338 --> 00:20:09.102
For the past several days,
we've been making every effort

00:20:09.174 --> 00:20:11.267
to recruit members
into an alliance,

00:20:11.343 --> 00:20:13.334
but it hasn't been easy.

00:20:13.412 --> 00:20:16.108
Whenever a new ship
gets pulled into the Void,

00:20:16.181 --> 00:20:17.944
they're immediately attacked.

00:20:18.016 --> 00:20:19.449
Instead of attacking it,

00:20:19.518 --> 00:20:22.316
you'd have to help
defend the new ship.

00:20:22.387 --> 00:20:24.617
And how is that in my interest?

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:27.523
It would encourage them
to join our alliance.

00:20:27.593 --> 00:20:31.359
And if they refuse,
then we raid them?

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.954
Everyone in the
alliance must agree

00:20:33.031 --> 00:20:35.192
not to launch
unprovoked attacks.

00:20:35.267 --> 00:20:37.758
Then how are we supposed
to get supplies?

00:20:37.836 --> 00:20:39.963
The idea is to recruit
new members,

00:20:40.105 --> 00:20:41.970
share technology and resources.

00:20:42.107 --> 00:20:44.632
We almost escaped the Void
on our own.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.770
If we work together,
I believe we'll succeed.

00:20:47.846 --> 00:20:51.179
How many ships do you have
in this alliance?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.115
You'd be the first.

00:20:53.185 --> 00:20:57.417
Technically, Captain,
that's not correct.

00:20:57.489 --> 00:20:59.616
I consider myself
the first member

00:20:59.691 --> 00:21:01.352
of the Captain's coalition.

00:21:01.426 --> 00:21:04.793
Six years ago,
I offered her my services

00:21:04.863 --> 00:21:05.921
and the resources of my ship,

00:21:06.064 --> 00:21:07.429
and she has never failed
to help me

00:21:07.499 --> 00:21:08.796
when I needed her.

00:21:08.867 --> 00:21:11.665
It's a noble idea, Captain,

00:21:11.737 --> 00:21:15.434
but good intentions are
like deuterium reserves...

00:21:15.507 --> 00:21:18.067
they tend to get lost
in the Void.

00:21:18.143 --> 00:21:21.237
All I ask is that you consider
our proposal.

00:21:21.313 --> 00:21:23.941
I will.

00:21:24.016 --> 00:21:25.881
In the meantime,

00:21:25.951 --> 00:21:28.681
we'd like to offer you
food and medical supplies.

00:21:28.754 --> 00:21:31.552
What do you expect in return?

00:21:31.623 --> 00:21:34.114
Nothing.

00:21:34.192 --> 00:21:36.183
Compliments of the alliance.

00:21:42.801 --> 00:21:44.701
I tried.

00:21:50.042 --> 00:21:51.407
Captain...

00:21:51.476 --> 00:21:52.500
there's been a theft.

00:21:52.577 --> 00:21:53.635
What's missing?

00:21:53.712 --> 00:21:54.644
My phase compensator.

00:21:54.713 --> 00:21:55.805
No doubt, it was stolen

00:21:55.881 --> 00:21:57.576
by one of your
prospective members.

00:21:57.649 --> 00:22:00.243
It wasn't stolen.
I gave it to the Nygeans.

00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.253
They needed it
to repair their sensor array.

00:22:02.321 --> 00:22:05.415
I presume you obtained something
equally valuable in return.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:06.923
I think I did.

00:22:06.992 --> 00:22:08.755
The goodwill
of a potential ally.

00:22:08.827 --> 00:22:10.089
Did they join?

00:22:10.162 --> 00:22:11.094
Not yet.

00:22:11.163 --> 00:22:13.597
- Captain...
- I know.

00:22:13.665 --> 00:22:16.327
It's not exactly
the most "efficient" policy.

00:22:16.401 --> 00:22:19.768
But, then, you don't always do
what's most efficient either.

00:22:19.838 --> 00:22:21.601
I don't know
what you're implying.

00:22:21.673 --> 00:22:24.608
You gave up your rations
to our guest in Sick Bay.

00:22:24.676 --> 00:22:26.109
He needed food.

00:22:26.178 --> 00:22:28.772
You're a valuable
member of this crew.

00:22:28.847 --> 00:22:29.814
Your friend in Sick Bay

00:22:29.881 --> 00:22:31.439
is nothing but a drain
on resources.

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:35.612
What's efficient about
wasting food on him?

00:22:35.687 --> 00:22:37.416
You think I'm being inefficient,

00:22:37.489 --> 00:22:39.616
Tuvok thinks
I'm being illogical...

00:22:39.691 --> 00:22:41.124
You both could be right.

00:22:41.193 --> 00:22:45.459
But maybe the best way
to get help is to give it.

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:46.963
Oh, and, Seven?

00:22:47.032 --> 00:22:48.659
- Yes?
- I'm sorry

00:22:48.734 --> 00:22:51.532
I gave away your favorite
phase compensator.

00:23:13.825 --> 00:23:15.087
How is he?

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.422
Much better.

00:23:16.495 --> 00:23:17.587
He seemed to relax
when he heard me

00:23:17.662 --> 00:23:19.095
humming an aria from Rigoletto,

00:23:19.164 --> 00:23:22.099
so I had the computer play
the full orchestral version.

00:23:22.167 --> 00:23:24.761
Fantome seems to be
a music lover.

00:23:24.836 --> 00:23:26.098
"Fantome"?

00:23:26.171 --> 00:23:27.604
After The Phantom of the Opera,

00:23:27.672 --> 00:23:30.766
a tormented character
who is soothed by music.

00:23:30.842 --> 00:23:33.675
In six years, you haven't chosen
a name for yourself,

00:23:33.745 --> 00:23:36.270
but you've given Fantome one
in a few days.

00:23:36.348 --> 00:23:37.280
Choosing the right name
for myself

00:23:37.349 --> 00:23:38.441
is extremely difficult.

00:23:38.517 --> 00:23:40.382
I'm a complex individual.

00:23:40.452 --> 00:23:41.942
And Fantome isn't?

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.282
On the contrary.

00:23:43.355 --> 00:23:45.050
I believe
he's quite intelligent,

00:23:45.123 --> 00:23:47.250
and his physiology's
very sophisticated.

00:23:47.325 --> 00:23:49.555
Did you know he has
the ability to refract

00:23:49.628 --> 00:23:50.595
his own life signs?

00:23:50.662 --> 00:23:51.629
That would explain

00:23:51.696 --> 00:23:53.288
why our sensors
didn't detect him.

00:23:55.267 --> 00:23:58.566
I wish we could find a way
to communicate with him.

00:23:58.637 --> 00:24:01.128
I suspect he'd have
a lot to tell us.

00:24:05.811 --> 00:24:07.244
We were enjoying that.

00:24:07.312 --> 00:24:08.609
Exactly.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:11.672
He may not be able to speak,
but he can hear.

00:24:36.508 --> 00:24:38.601
He understands.

00:24:41.947 --> 00:24:43.414
So it would seem.

00:24:51.823 --> 00:24:53.381
What's the occasion?

00:24:53.458 --> 00:24:55.255
Seven's not the only one

00:24:55.327 --> 00:24:58.057
who knows how
to set an elegant table.

00:24:58.129 --> 00:25:01.064
You have heard
there is a food shortage.

00:25:01.132 --> 00:25:02.394
That's no reason

00:25:02.467 --> 00:25:05.630
why you two can't enjoy
a romantic dinner.

00:25:07.339 --> 00:25:10.172
Unfortunately,
I can't light this.

00:25:10.242 --> 00:25:12.403
It would be a waste of oxygen.

00:25:12.477 --> 00:25:14.411
Still, it is festive.

00:25:14.479 --> 00:25:16.276
We appreciate the effort.

00:25:18.149 --> 00:25:20.811
I believe there's been
a mistake here, waiter.

00:25:20.886 --> 00:25:22.183
I didn't order this.

00:25:22.254 --> 00:25:27.351
Close your eyes and pretend that
it's Seven's fettran risotto.

00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:37.497
It tastes more like chicken.

00:25:40.906 --> 00:25:42.032
What's this?

00:25:42.107 --> 00:25:44.337
A preserved Olian guava.

00:25:44.409 --> 00:25:45.933
I had a few left.

00:25:46.044 --> 00:25:47.773
Neelix...

00:25:47.846 --> 00:25:50.144
No arguments.
You're eating for two.

00:25:50.215 --> 00:25:53.446
Senior officers,
report to stations immediately.

00:25:53.518 --> 00:25:54.780
Sorry, Neelix.

00:25:56.121 --> 00:25:58.055
Charge weapons.
Shields to full.

00:25:58.123 --> 00:25:59.055
What's going on?

00:25:59.124 --> 00:26:00.250
A funnel just opened.

00:26:00.325 --> 00:26:01.792
It pulled in a new vessel.

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:03.760
Two warships are approaching it.

00:26:03.828 --> 00:26:05.261
One of them is Valen's.

00:26:09.434 --> 00:26:11.163
Target Valen's weapons
and hail him.

00:26:14.272 --> 00:26:16.536
My fight's not with you,
Captain.

00:26:16.608 --> 00:26:18.303
Then stand down.

00:26:18.376 --> 00:26:21.573
This new ship has
impressive technology.

00:26:21.646 --> 00:26:23.170
We can share it.

00:26:23.248 --> 00:26:25.580
I'm not here
to divide the spoils.

00:26:25.650 --> 00:26:28.551
Then why are you here?

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:31.384
To protect the ship
you're firing on.

00:26:31.456 --> 00:26:33.424
What are they to you?

00:26:33.491 --> 00:26:35.425
Just some people
in a bad situation,

00:26:35.493 --> 00:26:37.154
like the rest of us.

00:26:37.228 --> 00:26:38.923
Save your speeches.

00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:41.294
I've got a crew to feed.

00:26:43.602 --> 00:26:44.330
He's targeting our shields.

00:26:44.402 --> 00:26:45.460
Take his weapons out.

00:26:45.537 --> 00:26:46.504
Hail the new ship.

00:26:49.074 --> 00:26:49.938
I surrender.

00:26:50.075 --> 00:26:51.440
We're here to help you.

00:26:51.509 --> 00:26:53.170
Can you target
the smaller warship?

00:26:53.244 --> 00:26:56.236
We're a survey vessel.
We're not equipped to fight.

00:26:57.782 --> 00:26:59.409
Shields at 60 percent.

00:26:59.484 --> 00:27:01.850
Fire torpedoes.

00:27:07.025 --> 00:27:09.823
Shields on Valen's lead ship
are holding at 80 percent.

00:27:09.894 --> 00:27:12.692
It appears he's upgraded them
since we last met.

00:27:12.764 --> 00:27:13.560
Ours?

00:27:13.632 --> 00:27:15.532
Thirty.

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:22.501
The smaller ship
is outmaneuvering us.

00:27:22.574 --> 00:27:26.101
We have hull breaches
on Decks 5 and 6.

00:27:26.177 --> 00:27:27.041
Seal them.

00:27:27.112 --> 00:27:30.047
Shields at 15 percent.

00:27:30.115 --> 00:27:32.345
- Engineering to the Bridge.
- Go ahead.

00:27:35.987 --> 00:27:37.579
We're losing containment.

00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:39.089
At this rate,
we'll be dead in the water

00:27:39.157 --> 00:27:41.523
in less than three minutes.

00:27:42.961 --> 00:27:44.189
We should retreat, Captain.

00:27:45.430 --> 00:27:46.863
Not yet.

00:27:46.931 --> 00:27:48.125
We might want to reconsider.

00:27:48.199 --> 00:27:49.632
There's another ship
approaching.

00:27:49.701 --> 00:27:51.794
We can't defend ourselves
against three ships.

00:27:51.870 --> 00:27:53.360
We may not have to.

00:27:53.438 --> 00:27:55.463
The third vessel
belongs to Mr. Garon.

00:27:55.540 --> 00:27:57.201
He's firing at the other two.

00:28:02.681 --> 00:28:04.308
Valen's shields are down.

00:28:04.382 --> 00:28:06.646
The smaller ship
is leaking plasma.

00:28:06.718 --> 00:28:08.379
They're both retreating.

00:28:08.453 --> 00:28:09.715
Garon's hailing.

00:28:09.788 --> 00:28:11.278
Get a weapons lock on him.

00:28:11.356 --> 00:28:13.950
We've been fooled
by unexpected allies before.

00:28:16.361 --> 00:28:17.885
Why are you targeting me?

00:28:17.996 --> 00:28:20.055
Because I don't know
what your intentions are.

00:28:20.131 --> 00:28:21.826
Haven't I just made them clear?

00:28:23.234 --> 00:28:26.067
I've decided
to accept your offer.

00:28:29.641 --> 00:28:30.938
Well, in that case...

00:28:32.010 --> 00:28:35.946
...welcome to the alliance.

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:43.246
Captain's Log, Stardate 54562.7.

00:28:43.321 --> 00:28:46.757
Since Garon and the survey ship
became our charter members,

00:28:46.825 --> 00:28:49.419
finding new allies
has gotten a little easier.

00:28:49.494 --> 00:28:52.759
My latest prospect
is Commander Bosaal,

00:28:52.831 --> 00:28:56.028
whose ship has technology
that could help us escape.

00:28:56.101 --> 00:28:58.626
Neelix, we have
another guest for dinner.

00:28:58.703 --> 00:29:01.604
Always room for one more,
Captain.

00:29:01.673 --> 00:29:04.540
Who did you raid
to get fresh vegetables?

00:29:04.609 --> 00:29:05.974
They're replicated.

00:29:06.044 --> 00:29:07.841
One of the crews that joined us

00:29:07.912 --> 00:29:11.006
had technology that tripled
our replicator efficiency.

00:29:11.082 --> 00:29:12.777
It may not be a gourmet feast,

00:29:12.851 --> 00:29:15.843
but we can feed
500 people a day now,

00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:18.980
using half the power
it took us a few days ago.

00:29:19.057 --> 00:29:21.753
Why don't we sit down?

00:29:30.468 --> 00:29:31.560
Doctor.

00:29:31.636 --> 00:29:32.728
Hello, Commander.

00:29:32.804 --> 00:29:34.237
How's your patient?

00:29:34.305 --> 00:29:36.330
Technically, he's not
a patient anymore,

00:29:36.407 --> 00:29:37.999
but it's taken me
this long to coax him

00:29:38.076 --> 00:29:39.008
out of Sick Bay.

00:29:39.077 --> 00:29:40.567
He's quite shy.

00:29:40.645 --> 00:29:44.046
I'm telling him not to worry...

00:29:44.115 --> 00:29:46.845
that you're the one
who keeps us all safe.

00:29:48.153 --> 00:29:49.711
He says, "Thank you."

00:29:49.788 --> 00:29:52.552
An ingenious method
of communication.

00:29:52.624 --> 00:29:54.148
It began
with a few simple words,

00:29:54.225 --> 00:29:56.625
but now we're capable
of rudimentary conversation.

00:29:56.694 --> 00:29:58.321
Tell him I'm pleased
he's feeling better.

00:29:58.396 --> 00:29:59.328
I will.

00:30:16.281 --> 00:30:19.717
What's that parasite
doing aboard your ship?

00:30:22.587 --> 00:30:24.612
I beg your pardon?

00:30:24.689 --> 00:30:26.384
They're vermin.

00:30:26.457 --> 00:30:28.288
I don't know who you are, sir,

00:30:28.359 --> 00:30:30.759
but your choice of words
is offensive.

00:30:30.829 --> 00:30:32.353
What is offensive is the way

00:30:32.430 --> 00:30:34.625
they slip aboard
during transport,

00:30:34.699 --> 00:30:38.260
hide in conduits,
steal food, spread disease.

00:30:38.336 --> 00:30:40.566
Fantome is perfectly healthy,

00:30:40.638 --> 00:30:43.266
and unlike some people
in this Void, he hasn't stolen

00:30:43.341 --> 00:30:45.206
anything.

00:30:45.276 --> 00:30:48.143
If my sensors could detect
where they are on my ship,

00:30:48.213 --> 00:30:49.373
I'd exterminate them.

00:30:49.447 --> 00:30:51.972
I suggest you do the same.

00:30:52.083 --> 00:30:53.141
Captain, this is outrageous!

00:30:53.218 --> 00:30:54.207
Doctor!

00:31:00.792 --> 00:31:02.282
One of the principles
of our alliance

00:31:02.360 --> 00:31:04.328
is that we don't discriminate.

00:31:04.395 --> 00:31:06.022
Everyone's welcome,

00:31:06.097 --> 00:31:08.827
as long as they
follow the rules.

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:11.095
But if you're having
a bad experience

00:31:11.169 --> 00:31:14.229
with the members of this species
on your ship,

00:31:14.305 --> 00:31:17.797
I'd be happy to bring
them to Voyager.

00:31:17.876 --> 00:31:19.810
If you could find them.

00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:23.780
Now that we've had a chance to
analyze Fantome's physiology,

00:31:23.848 --> 00:31:26.840
I think we can get
a transporter lock on them.

00:31:26.918 --> 00:31:31.514
Is this your way of enticing me
to join your... alliance?

00:31:31.589 --> 00:31:33.614
I'm simply trying to demonstrate

00:31:33.691 --> 00:31:37.058
how cooperation and tolerance
can benefit everyone.

00:31:38.129 --> 00:31:41.223
Then we have an agreement.

00:31:46.204 --> 00:31:50.106
Okay, now connect
the primary emitter relay.

00:31:52.477 --> 00:31:53.967
On line.

00:31:54.045 --> 00:31:55.239
How is it coming?

00:31:55.313 --> 00:31:56.245
Pretty well.

00:31:56.314 --> 00:31:57.679
We just need to...

00:31:59.250 --> 00:32:01.411
I guess I was being
a little optimistic.

00:32:01.486 --> 00:32:02.885
What's the problem, exactly?

00:32:02.954 --> 00:32:05.013
Uh, we think we can establish
a shield bubble

00:32:05.089 --> 00:32:06.920
large enough to encompass
all our ships,

00:32:06.991 --> 00:32:09.084
but we have no way to compensate
for the graviton stress.

00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:12.425
Wouldn't a polaron modulator
be able to do that?

00:32:12.497 --> 00:32:13.930
Unfortunately, nobody
in the alliance has one.

00:32:13.998 --> 00:32:16.558
We've been trying to build
our own, but so far...

00:32:16.634 --> 00:32:18.659
Maybe we could trade
for one, or find

00:32:18.736 --> 00:32:19.896
a new ally who has one.

00:32:19.971 --> 00:32:21.939
Well, it's not a common piece
of technology,

00:32:22.006 --> 00:32:22.938
and it's valuable.

00:32:23.007 --> 00:32:24.634
It may be difficult
to convince anyone

00:32:24.709 --> 00:32:25.835
to part with it.

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:27.844
You never know unless you ask...

00:32:27.912 --> 00:32:28.936
You are not authorized
to be in here.

00:32:29.013 --> 00:32:31.607
We're making a valuable
contribution to the alliance.

00:32:31.683 --> 00:32:33.844
By spying
on restricted meetings?

00:32:33.918 --> 00:32:37.752
We've devised a new
surveillance technique.

00:32:37.822 --> 00:32:39.483
Ask Harry to give you a...

00:32:39.557 --> 00:32:41.184
You've bypassed
my security measures.

00:32:41.259 --> 00:32:44.558
We can observe activity
on any ship in the Void

00:32:44.629 --> 00:32:46.221
without being detected.

00:32:46.297 --> 00:32:49.698
This is the cargo hold
on the Jelinian freighter.

00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:53.328
Now, if I'm not mistaken,
the Jelinians

00:32:53.404 --> 00:32:54.894
are a member of our alliance.

00:32:54.973 --> 00:32:58.204
Which is why you shouldn't
be spying on them.

00:32:58.276 --> 00:33:01.336
And why they shouldn't
be hoarding their ale.

00:33:43.621 --> 00:33:44.849
Lovely piece.

00:33:44.922 --> 00:33:46.856
Did they compose it, or did you?

00:33:46.924 --> 00:33:48.255
They did.

00:33:48.326 --> 00:33:50.089
Though strictly speaking,
it's not a composition.

00:33:50.161 --> 00:33:52.322
It's more of a conversation.

00:33:52.397 --> 00:33:53.625
I'm impressed.

00:33:53.698 --> 00:33:54.960
I wish I could take credit,

00:33:55.033 --> 00:33:56.557
but it was Fantome
who taught the others

00:33:56.634 --> 00:33:58.966
in a fraction of the time
it took him to learn.

00:33:59.037 --> 00:34:00.800
They're a highly
intelligent species.

00:34:00.872 --> 00:34:02.066
The language is
already developing

00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:04.233
its own grammar and syntax.

00:34:04.308 --> 00:34:06.742
That suggests they have
a language of their own.

00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:09.245
Mm-hmm. It could be
telepathic, but they seem

00:34:09.313 --> 00:34:14.046
just as comfortable
communicating with music now.

00:34:14.118 --> 00:34:16.609
Could their species be native
to the Void?

00:34:16.687 --> 00:34:17.915
It's certainly possible.

00:34:17.989 --> 00:34:19.718
They told us
they were born here.

00:34:19.791 --> 00:34:22.453
Just when you think
nothing in the galaxy

00:34:22.527 --> 00:34:24.324
can surprise you anymore...

00:34:24.395 --> 00:34:28.354
Captain Janeway, please report
to Engineering.

00:34:33.771 --> 00:34:35.796
Just what we needed, Captain...

00:34:35.873 --> 00:34:38.433
a fully compatible
polaron modulator.

00:34:38.509 --> 00:34:39.942
Where did you get it?

00:34:40.044 --> 00:34:41.875
A Kinjal frigate.

00:34:41.946 --> 00:34:43.811
Do they want to join
our alliance?

00:34:43.881 --> 00:34:46.213
They're not interested.

00:34:48.319 --> 00:34:50.310
How did you get this?

00:34:50.388 --> 00:34:51.650
I traded for it.

00:34:51.722 --> 00:34:53.485
What did you give them?

00:34:55.026 --> 00:34:56.994
I don't answer to you.

00:34:58.529 --> 00:35:01.430
Did you steal it?

00:35:05.002 --> 00:35:07.095
Disconnect the modulator.

00:35:07.171 --> 00:35:08.433
Captain?

00:35:08.506 --> 00:35:10.838
We're returning it
to the people it belongs to.

00:35:10.908 --> 00:35:14.173
They have no more use for it.

00:35:14.245 --> 00:35:15.735
You don't know that.

00:35:15.813 --> 00:35:20.341
Yes... I do.

00:35:20.418 --> 00:35:22.283
You killed them...

00:35:22.353 --> 00:35:23.684
Captain.

00:35:23.754 --> 00:35:26.188
I don't like his tactics
any more than you do,

00:35:26.257 --> 00:35:29.249
but why waste this technology
when we're so close to escaping?

00:35:29.327 --> 00:35:30.589
Because it's a violation

00:35:30.661 --> 00:35:32.652
of everything
this alliance stands for.

00:35:32.730 --> 00:35:34.561
Refusing the modulator
won't bring back

00:35:34.632 --> 00:35:35.690
the people he killed.

00:35:35.766 --> 00:35:40.601
No, but using it would make us
accessories to murder.

00:35:40.671 --> 00:35:42.696
Take it and get out.

00:36:11.969 --> 00:36:14.733
The Jelinians and the Kraylor
have left with Bosaal.

00:36:14.805 --> 00:36:16.238
They felt you were being...

00:36:16.307 --> 00:36:18.241
Impulsive and self-righteous?

00:36:18.309 --> 00:36:19.901
Is that what you think?

00:36:19.977 --> 00:36:21.911
You did what you had to do.

00:36:21.979 --> 00:36:23.412
Still, I made a mistake.

00:36:23.481 --> 00:36:25.142
By telling Bosaal to leave?

00:36:25.216 --> 00:36:26.911
Allowing him to join
in the first place.

00:36:26.984 --> 00:36:28.508
You couldn't have known
what he was going to do.

00:36:28.586 --> 00:36:31.054
Oh, I had a pretty good idea
what kind of person he was.

00:36:31.122 --> 00:36:33.420
That bigoted reaction he had
to the Doctor's friend

00:36:33.491 --> 00:36:37.757
told me all I needed to know,
but I ignored my instincts.

00:36:37.828 --> 00:36:38.920
Why?

00:36:38.996 --> 00:36:41.521
Because I thought his ship
could help us escape.

00:36:41.599 --> 00:36:44.261
You weren't the only one
who wanted him in the alliance.

00:36:44.335 --> 00:36:46.269
Maybe not...
but if I'd listened

00:36:46.337 --> 00:36:47.895
to my doubts in the first place,

00:36:47.972 --> 00:36:50.236
we wouldn't have lost
the other two ships.

00:36:50.308 --> 00:36:51.935
We'll find a way out
of here without them.

00:36:52.009 --> 00:36:53.442
Where do we stand
with the modulator?

00:36:53.511 --> 00:36:55.172
B'Elanna and the other engineers

00:36:55.246 --> 00:36:57.214
are working around
the clock to build one.

00:36:57.281 --> 00:37:00.580
She thinks they'll be ready
to test in a couple of days.

00:37:00.651 --> 00:37:03.711
So everyone's pulling together
to make up for my mistake?

00:37:03.788 --> 00:37:04.880
They have to.

00:37:04.956 --> 00:37:07.390
It says so
in the Federation Charter.

00:37:08.726 --> 00:37:10.660
Good news, I hope.

00:37:10.728 --> 00:37:12.161
I'm afraid not.

00:37:12.230 --> 00:37:13.595
It appears Commander Bosaal

00:37:13.664 --> 00:37:15.996
is attempting to form
an alliance of his own

00:37:16.067 --> 00:37:18.001
with one of our adversaries.

00:37:18.069 --> 00:37:20.094
We recorded a tactical
conversation

00:37:20.171 --> 00:37:23.265
that took place between them
just a few minutes ago.

00:37:23.341 --> 00:37:25.901
Don't underestimate Janeway.

00:37:25.977 --> 00:37:28.070
I've been in battle
with her twice.

00:37:28.145 --> 00:37:30.375
Then you know Janeway's tactics.

00:37:30.448 --> 00:37:32.006
I have two other ships.

00:37:32.083 --> 00:37:35.644
We can take Voyager's
food and weapons

00:37:35.720 --> 00:37:37.483
if we work together.

00:37:37.555 --> 00:37:39.648
The rest of their
conversation suggests

00:37:39.724 --> 00:37:41.817
they will attack
within the next 48 hours.

00:37:41.892 --> 00:37:44.759
I'm so glad we taught them
the value of cooperation.

00:37:44.829 --> 00:37:47.696
Our power reserves
will be severely depleted

00:37:47.765 --> 00:37:49.130
if we're forced
to defend ourselves.

00:37:50.534 --> 00:37:53.662
Tell B'Elanna we don't have time
to test her modulator.

00:37:53.738 --> 00:37:55.933
We've got to try to escape now.

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:04.110
Sorry to interrupt, but we've
got a situation developing.

00:38:05.850 --> 00:38:08.410
We're going to try
to break free of the anomaly.

00:38:08.486 --> 00:38:10.181
Your friends are welcome
to join us,

00:38:10.254 --> 00:38:12.245
but they should be aware
of the dangers.

00:38:16.260 --> 00:38:17.420
The Void's their home.

00:38:17.495 --> 00:38:18.427
They want to stay.

00:38:18.496 --> 00:38:20.794
Where would they like us
to transport them?

00:38:20.865 --> 00:38:21.889
They're nomads.

00:38:22.033 --> 00:38:23.295
Any ship will do.

00:38:26.037 --> 00:38:28.301
They say they're grateful
for our help.

00:38:30.041 --> 00:38:31.975
They want to help us now.

00:39:46.717 --> 00:39:49.117
There's a funnel forming
in Grid 4.

00:39:49.186 --> 00:39:51.017
Graviton surge in 98 seconds.

00:39:51.088 --> 00:39:53.056
Alert the other ships.

00:39:54.425 --> 00:39:56.188
Take us in, Tom.

00:39:56.260 --> 00:39:57.557
Aye, Captain.

00:39:57.628 --> 00:39:59.721
Bosaal and his fleet
are approaching.

00:39:59.797 --> 00:40:01.321
They are charging weapons.

00:40:01.399 --> 00:40:02.730
Janeway to Engineering.

00:40:02.800 --> 00:40:03.732
Status.

00:40:03.801 --> 00:40:05.598
I need two more minutes.

00:40:05.669 --> 00:40:07.296
You've got one.

00:40:14.311 --> 00:40:16.245
Surge in 50 seconds!

00:40:16.313 --> 00:40:18.611
Voyager to all alliance ships.

00:40:18.682 --> 00:40:21.116
Begin firing
at your designated targets.

00:40:28.659 --> 00:40:30.718
We've penetrated shields
on both vessels.

00:40:30.795 --> 00:40:32.319
Janeway to the Doctor.

00:40:32.396 --> 00:40:33.761
Initiate transport.

00:40:33.831 --> 00:40:35.662
Acknowledged.

00:40:38.269 --> 00:40:40.237
Yes. Good-bye and good luck.

00:40:41.605 --> 00:40:43.539
Energize.

00:40:48.245 --> 00:40:50.509
Transport complete, Captain.

00:40:50.581 --> 00:40:53.106
They're in the engine rooms
of both ships.

00:40:53.184 --> 00:40:54.242
Acknowledged.

00:40:54.318 --> 00:40:56.752
30 seconds.

00:40:56.821 --> 00:40:59.312
Janeway to Engineering.
We need that modulator.

00:40:59.390 --> 00:41:01.085
Just a few more seconds.

00:41:09.166 --> 00:41:11.930
We're receiving a hail
from Valen's ship... audio only.

00:41:12.002 --> 00:41:13.264
Let's hear it.

00:41:15.339 --> 00:41:16.931
What's he saying, Doctor?

00:41:18.342 --> 00:41:19.673
Mission accomplished.

00:41:19.743 --> 00:41:22.143
Fantome shut down power
on Valen's ship.

00:41:22.213 --> 00:41:23.180
Confirmed.

00:41:23.247 --> 00:41:25.511
Bosaal's ship
has lost power, as well.

00:41:25.583 --> 00:41:28.450
Who says gremlins
in the engine are a myth.

00:41:28.519 --> 00:41:29.781
Surge in five seconds...

00:41:29.854 --> 00:41:30.786
four...

00:41:30.855 --> 00:41:32.152
Now, B'Elanna.

00:41:39.797 --> 00:41:41.856
All ships are in formation.

00:41:42.933 --> 00:41:45.231
Structural integrity
at 30 percent.

00:41:45.302 --> 00:41:47.600
40,000 meters to normal space.

00:41:50.674 --> 00:41:52.437
Twenty percent.

00:41:52.510 --> 00:41:54.034
Ten percent.

00:41:56.947 --> 00:41:58.244
Do it, Tom.

00:42:08.592 --> 00:42:12.494
Gentlemen, it's been a privilege
to have you as allies.

00:42:12.563 --> 00:42:14.497
I never believed we'd escape.

00:42:14.565 --> 00:42:16.499
Then why did you join?

00:42:16.567 --> 00:42:19.297
Captain Janeway
is very persuasive,

00:42:19.370 --> 00:42:20.928
and the food was good.

00:42:21.071 --> 00:42:23.403
You're welcome to have
a meal with us anytime.

00:42:23.474 --> 00:42:26.272
Ah, unfortunately, we're headed
in the opposite direction.

00:42:26.343 --> 00:42:28.573
Safe journey to you
and your crew, Captain.

00:42:28.646 --> 00:42:30.273
And to all of yours, as well.

00:42:30.347 --> 00:42:31.939
Thank you.

00:42:45.296 --> 00:42:49.232
It was almost like being part
of the Federation again.

00:42:49.300 --> 00:42:52.428
The real one's only
30,000 light-years away.

00:42:52.503 --> 00:42:54.733
Then what are we
standing around for?
